OL,0,       G351 HBN TEKSTI-TVG25.11.06:25:50
OL,1,V $WW]D     WEEKLY ALBUM REVIEW      2/4
OL,2,V!1!U]    G        KRIS                 
OL,3,V $$                                    
OL,4,CM       Revolver, The Beatles          
OL,6,           C Released:1966              
OL,7, Let me get this out of the way first;  
OL,8, half a star off because I usually only 
OL,9, reserve 5 stars for my all-time        
OL,10, favorites. though this album, for me,  
OL,11, is very very close to the greatest     
OL,12, ones.                                  
OL,14, There is something very strange in this
OL,15, album that no other Beatles record has.
OL,16, A sort of trance or dream-like state   
OL,17, that I always feel very deeply while   
OL,18, listening to Revolver.                 
OL,22,                          C         >>> 
FL,0,0,0,0,0,100
PN,35103
SC,0003
PS,C100
CT,20,T
OL,0,       G351 HBN TEKSTI-TVG25.11.06:25:50
OL,1,V $WW]D     WEEKLY ALBUM REVIEW      3/4
OL,2,V!1!U]    G        KRIS                 
OL,3,V $$                                    
OL,4, Each track has its own vibe but there's
OL,5, a melancholy atmosphere in all of them,
OL,6, in some songs even so melancholy that  
OL,7, it's hauntingly beautiful (for example,
OL,8, "I'm Only Sleeping" and "She Said She  
OL,9, Said").                                
OL,11, People often talk about Sgt. Pepper's  
OL,12, Lonely Hearts Club Band being the      
OL,13, Beatles' most unique, one-of-a-kind    
OL,14, work. I absolutely agree. However, each
OL,15, time I re-listen to Revolver, I start  
OL,16, noticing more and more how separate    
OL,17, this album is from the rest of their   
OL,18, discography. I might be just hearing   
OL,19, things, since Rubber Soul had a few    
OL,20, similarities, but not to this degree I 
OL,21, don't think.                           
OL,22,                          C         >>> 
FL,0,0,0,0,0,100
PN,35104
SC,0004
PS,C100
CT,20,T
OL,0,       G351 HBN TEKSTI-TVG25.11.06:25:50
OL,1,V $WW]D     WEEKLY ALBUM REVIEW      4/4
OL,2,V!1!U]    G        KRIS                 
OL,3,V $$                                    
OL,4, This is very difficult to explain to   
OL,5, someone who hasn't grown up listening  
OL,6, to The Beatles. I can hear it the way a
OL,7, newbie probably would, this sounds like
OL,8, most other psychedelic rock from the   
OL,9, 60s. But no matter how many different  
OL,10, obscure 60s psychedelic albums I listen
OL,11, to, or any other classics, I have never
OL,12, heard a sound quite like Revolver.     
OL,14, This album has a very special place in 
OL,15, my heart.                              
OL,16, ---------------------------------------
